From 6981b8700218c5da672565420aee0f958f30cf3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden-Doris <doris@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:42:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Eden (Doris): emulator threads on the middle cores;
 Eden's CPU topology from all cores; shader builders not background

A TotK log (release 35, ClusterTune Medium) showed busy areas (3000-4600 draws a frame) at 17-22 fps
with the GPU 50-75% busy and Eden's GPU emulation thread 63-87% busy: that thread is the limit there.
Eden read its CPU topology at minute 12, at a moment Android had the app in a cpuset without the
prime core, and kept that for the rest of the session.
- The topology now comes from all the CPUs (masks naming CPUs outside the current cpuset are fine,
  the kernel uses the allowed part), so it no longer depends on that moment.
- The GPU thread and the other heavy emulator threads (emulated CPU cores, Vulkan worker,
  presentation, fences, timing) are kept on the middle cores: never on the little cores, where they
  are slow, and not on the prime core, which runs hotter (through Eden's core groups, which its
  policy refresh keeps). Where they ran for most of that session, without the trips to the little
  cores.
- With asynchronous shaders off the game waits for every new pipeline, so the pipeline builders run
  at normal priority on the performance cores instead of as background threads.
Thread placement only: nothing that is drawn changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
